1
00:00:00,500 --> 00:00:08,000
At the geographic and historical heart of Russia, the brick towers and gilded cathedrals of the Moscow Kremlin command the bend of the Moskva River.

2
00:00:08,500 --> 00:00:16,500
Outside the Spasskaya Tower lies Red Square, anchored by the iconic patterned onion domes of the 16th-century Saint Basil’s Cathedral.

3
00:00:17,000 --> 00:00:25,000
Centuries of defense shaped Moscow’s unique urban anatomy, radiating outward in concentric defensive belts.

4
00:00:25,500 --> 00:00:33,500
Following the fire of 1812, the medieval stone walls of the White City were transformed into the tree-lined Boulevard Ring.

5
00:00:34,000 --> 00:00:42,000
Further outward lies the sixteen-kilometer Garden Ring, tracing the ancient earthen ramparts built under Boris Godunov.

6
00:00:42,500 --> 00:00:50,500
In the 20th century, monumental Stalinist skyscrapers like the Kotelnicheskaya Embankment Building punctuated the skyline.

7
00:00:51,000 --> 00:00:59,500
From medieval citadel to radial modern metropolis, Moscow’s geometry stands as an enduring map of time and ambition.
